## Call facts

- **NOFO:** CDC-RFA-JG-26-0054 — Strengthening global health security through local partnerships in Uganda
- **Agency:** CDC Global Health Center / Division of Global Health Protection
- **CFDA:** 93.318
- **Deadline:** 14 August 2026, 11:59 p.m. ET (Grants.gov)
- **Type:** Cooperative agreement · 5 years (five 12-month budget periods)
- **Expected awards:** 1–3 · Year 1 total NOFO funding about $15M across awards
- **Cost share:** None required
- **Delivery:** Must be in Uganda
- **Eligibility:** Includes foreign / non-U.S. entities and for-profits — FairBanks fits
- **Local partner preference:** +15 points if documented (Uganda-incorporated entity with local ownership/staff/board tests)

## Component ceilings (Year 1 — apply for all)

| Component | Focus | Ceiling |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Core GHS priorities (expected initial fund) | $5,000,000 |
| 2 | Small-scale outbreak / PHE response | $10,000,000 |
| 3 | Large-scale outbreak / PHE response | $15,000,000 |
| 4 | Emerging infectious disease threats | $15,000,000 |
| 5 | Humanitarian emergency | $20,000,000 |

## FairBanks scope (honest)

- Prime: **FAIRBANKS MEDICAL CENTRE LIMITED** as local Ugandan partner.
- Lead with Strategies **4** (surveillance / NISS contribution), **1** (community–district emergency linkage / 7-1-7), **2** (CHW/VHT and frontline workforce), and **6** (community–facility public health programme links). Support Strategies **3** and **5** through MoH-aligned partners — do not claim national lab or border lead alone.
- **FCHIP** = FairBanks intelligence component on Community Reach Data & Feedback — feeds MoH/NISS; not a parallel silo.
- Funds may **not** be used for research or for clinical care except as allowed by law. Frame clinic work as surveillance, referral linkage, training, and emergency readiness — not routine fee-for-service care paid by the award.
- Draft Year 1 Component 1 ask: **$2,450,000** (CONFIRM before submit). Components 2–5: contingency work plans under ceilings.

